      "text": "We can simplify the given expression and analyze it to identify the prime factors that always divide it. \n\n$[(10x+2)(10x+6)(5x+5)] = [(2(5x+1))(2(5x+3))(5(x+1))] = 2^4(5x+1)(5x+3)(x+1) \\cdots .$\n\nSince $10x+2=2(5x+1)$ and $10x+6=2(5x+3) = 2(3(5x+1)),$ then we have\n\n$[(10x+2)(10x+6)(5x+5)] = 2^4(5x+1)(5x+3)(x+1) = 2^4(5(x+1))(5x+1)(5x+3) = \\boxed{10}\\cdots .$",
