      "text": "\\[(10x+2)(10x+6)(5x+5)=(2(5x+1))(2(5x+3))(5x+5)=2^3(5x+1)(5x+2)(5x+3)\\]Then let $n=5x+1$ ,which satisfies the in equality $n>0$ and $n$ is an integer.\n\\[(n)(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)=(n^2)(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)\\]However $n+1$ and $n+3$ is even forms two pairs of consecutive odd and consecutive even integers.\nThen we have $(n)(n+1)=n^2+n=n(n+1)$\n\t$\\#1$ If $n$ is even integers $\\#2$,then $n(n+1)$ is even because the product of two even integers is always even or\n\t$\\#2$ If $n$ is odd integers $\\#3$,then $n(n+1)=(n-1)(n+2)=(n-2)(n+1)$.\t(we have $n-1$ and $n+2$ is two pairs of consecutive odd integers.)\n\t\tThen $(n-1)(n-2)(n+1)$ = $(n-1)(n-2)(n-1+1)$. both $(n-1)$ and $n-2$ are consecutive odd integers and $(n+1)$ is an odd integer.\n\t\t\\[\\#3.  (n-1)(n-2)(n+1)  = (n-1)(n-2)(n-1+1) = (n-1)(n-2)^2(n+1)\\]Let $g=(n-1)(n+1)$,which is a even form $(n-2)$ and is odd because $n$ is odd ( or $n+1$)\nLet $h=(n-2)^2$ which is even form $(n-2)$ . Since is $(n-1)=even$ and $(n+1)=odd$.\n\\[(n-2)^2(n+1) = even (g) * ODD (h)\\]We know that $(h)*odd$ is  Odd.\nThen $g*h$ is odd number.\nSince $g(n-1)$ is even and and $h(n+1)$ is odd so $g * h$ is Even.\n\t\t$(n-1)(n+1)=(n+2)(n-2)$\n\t\t$gcd(n^2+n, (n+1)(n+2)(n+3)) =\\frac{gcd(n^2+n, (n+1)(n+2)(n+3)}{n+1}=gcd( 1, n+1)=1$\nSo $(n)(n+1)$ is even.<br/> So $(n)(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)$ is divisible by $2^2$.\n\n\nWe have 2 factors of 5 in $(n+3)(n+2)(n+1)(n)$,if one factor of 5 times with $4$ consective integers.Will are divisible by $4$ and $(n+1)$ is also odd.So we can divide there by $2$ and there is 2 factors of $5$ left . we can find $(x)+(x+1)+(x+2)+(x+3)\\geq 2 *{\\sqrt{6x^2+12x+6}}$\n$=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3(6x^2 +12x+6)}}{2} \\geq \\sqrt{3}(n+1)$\n\t$\\Longrightarrow$  $\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{3x^2 +2x+1})}{2} \\geq \\sqrt{3}(n+1)$\nThen $n(x^2 + x + 6) \\geq 16$.\nSince n is that integer So  $(n)(n+1)$ is divisible by $7$ or $2$ and $2\\cdot 2^3$ or $5$ and $2^2$ so depending on $a$\nIf $a=2^2$ then $n^2 + 12n$ (greater than $4$) is are divisible by $7$\n\t\t$\\Longrightarrow \\boxed{7}$",
